From d71c1b824ec1eef11f90e23aa27329327dda86bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 06:16:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Finish redesign rollout: remaining screens, global palette
 unification
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Restyle the remaining screens still on the old look: driver Activity
  (fleet-style stat cards), Trip Detail (shared by driver and owner, teal
  route/markers per the map colour spec), driver inspection capture,
  owner reference-photos capture, owner driver detail, and the owner
  Vehicle Health Report screen — all now sit on the nude background with
  cardGreen/gold accents instead of the old off-white/dark-green look.
- Rebuild FleetDriverCard and the owner Home summary strip as cardGreen
  surfaces so Owner Home matches the rest of the redesigned app.
- Retire the old dark-forest-green palette everywhere else in one sweep:
  brandColors.darkGreen/green/errorRed call sites across every remaining
  screen and shared component now resolve to deep/emerald/alert, and the
  shared Paper theme's primary/background/error follow the same tokens
  (background is now the nude paper tone app-wide). mintGreen is left
  alone — it's only used by the illustrative SVG shot-guide diagrams.
